Seed the oscillator phase RNGs, so renders are reproducible

Oscillator::start() randomises each note's initial phase from a static
juce::Random, and juce::Random's default constructor seeds from the clock --
so no two renders of the same song are bit-identical, which rules out
regression-testing the renderer.

The random phase itself is the right behaviour (unison voices starting in
phase collapse into one louder voice), so only the seed becomes fixed: the
phases still spread, in the same way every run.

--- a/modules/tracktion_engine/utilities/tracktion_Oscillators.cpp
+++ b/modules/tracktion_engine/utilities/tracktion_Oscillators.cpp
@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@
 //==============================================================================
 void Oscillator::start()
 {
-    static juce::Random r;
+    static juce::Random r (1);   // fixed seed: reproducible renders (carve)
     phase = r.nextFloat();
 }
 
@@ -204,7 +204,7 @@
 
 void MultiVoiceOscillator::start()
 {
-    static juce::Random r;
+    static juce::Random r (2);   // fixed seed: reproducible renders (carve)
 
     for (int i = 0; i < oscillators.size(); i += 2)
     {
